Z||000004||88CoupeV6||10-23-2001||05:01 PM||||Yes, The fiero uses a 5 lugs on 100 mm center Bolt Pattern<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newsig.jpg">    <BR>:D  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000005||TRiAD||10-23-2001||05:09 PM||||Anyone know the offset requirements for him, so he doesn't look like a roller skate?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg"> <BR><I>Photoshop rendering of planned exterior modifications.</I>||||reg||1
Z||000006||FieroBUZZ||10-23-2001||05:46 PM||||You'll want an offset of about 36 to 40 mm.  The probable reason for the different size tires is that the narrower front tire is easier to manhandle with no power steering. I think it looks better as well.   You can go wider for the rear but much over 215 in the front will get you 'Popeye' arms.If you do a search for 'whells that fit' or such you'll find lists of stock wheels that will fit your car.<BR>Gary||||reg||1
Z||000007||Turkey on Rye||10-23-2001||06:30 PM||||I wanted to thank you guys for helping me with this. Its great to meet people that know what they are talking about. I'll keep you posted on what happens. Thanx again!<BR>        -Chris||||reg||1
